                "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 24 at 12:24PM MDT until September 25 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central, east central, and southeast New\nMexico, including the following areas, in central New Mexico,\nEastern Lincoln County and South Central Mountains. In east central\nNew Mexico, Curry County, De Baca County, Quay County and Roosevelt\nCounty. In southeast New Mexico, Chaves County Plains and Southwest\nChaves County.\n\n* WHEN...Through late tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Rounds of showers and storms will continue through tonight.\nRainfall rates up to 2 inches per hour will have the potential to\nproduce rapid runoff, especially during the afternoon and evening\nhours on Thursday. Soils are becoming increasingly saturated from\npersistent rainfall over the past couple of days, further\nelevating the risk of flash flooding. Rainfall amounts will\ngenerally range from 1 to 2 inches, with isolated totals up to 3\ninches.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
