                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 24 at 4:48AM HST until September 26 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "Intensifying Tropical Storm Nolo is expected to bring heavy flooding\nrain to the eastern end of the state over the next few days. The\nexact track of the dangerous tropical cyclone remains somewhat\nuncertain, but significant heavy rain is likely over windward and\nsoutheast Big Island.\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Big Island, Maui, Lanai, Molokai, and Kahoolawe.\n\n* WHEN...Through Saturday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Significant flooding may occur due to the overflow of\nstreams and drainages. Roads in several areas may be closed, along\nwith property damage in urban or low lying spots due to runoff.\nLandslides may also occur in areas with steep terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Deep moisture on the north side of Nolo will bring heavy showers\nlater today and tonight over Big Island and spread to Maui.\nWindward and southeast Big Island and windward Maui are the most\nlikely to experience heavy rain due to the slow moving tropical\ncyclone, with considerable flooding possible over portions of Big\nIsland Friday and Saturday. Other islands in Maui County are at\nrisk as well.",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
